24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C01
Reverse Unicode code points
Reverse the code points in a non-null string. State whether this preserves displayed
grapheme clusters.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Convert to code points, then append them in reverse order. This preserves surrogate pairs.
Combining marks and joined emoji need a separate grapheme-aware requirement.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static String reverseCodePoints(String s) {
    Objects.requireNonNull(s);
    int[] cp = s.codePoints().toArray();
    StringBuilder out = new StringBuilder();
    for (int i = cp.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
        out.appendCodePoint(cp[i]);
    }
    return out.toString();
}
Worked result: Input: A + U+1F600 + B. Output: B + U+1F600 + A.
Time and space: O(n) time and O(n) extra space, measured in code points.
Edge-case policy: Empty input returns empty. Null rejects. Code-point reversal is not grapheme reversal.
