24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C05
Balanced brackets with a stack
Check (), [] and {} nesting. Reject every other character under this input contract.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Push each opening bracket. For each closing bracket, compare with the most recent opening bracket.
At the end the stack must be empty.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static boolean balanced(String s) {
    Deque<Character> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();
    for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
        if (c == '(' || c == '[' || c == '{') stack.push(c);
        else {
            char expected;
            if (c == ')') expected = '(';
            else if (c == ']') expected = '[';
            else if (c == '}') expected = '{';
            else return false;
            if (stack.isEmpty() || stack.pop() != expected) return false;
        }
    }
    return stack.isEmpty();
}
Worked result: "{[()]}" returns true; "([)]" returns false.
Time and space: O(n) time and O(n) worst-case stack space.
Edge-case policy: Empty input is balanced. A leading closing bracket fails without popping an empty stack.
