24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C06
Binary search without midpoint overflow
Find a target index in a sorted ascending int array, or return -1.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Maintain an inclusive search range. Each comparison discards half the range. The input must already
satisfy the sorted-order precondition.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static int binarySearch(int[] a, int target) {
    int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1;
    while (lo <= hi) {
        int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (a[mid] == target) return mid;
        if (a[mid] < target) lo = mid + 1;
        else hi = mid - 1;
    }
    return -1;
}
Worked result: [1,3,5,7], target 5 gives index 2; target 6 gives -1.
Time and space: O(log n) time, O(1) extra space.
Edge-case policy: Empty array returns -1. For duplicates, this version returns any matching index.
