24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C07
Two sum with overflow-safe complements
Return two different indices whose integer values sum to a target, or an empty array.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
For each value, search earlier values for a complement. Calculate the complement using long and
only cast when it fits int, avoiding a false match caused by overflow.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static int[] twoSum(int[] a, int target) {
    Map<Integer, Integer> seen = new HashMap<>();
    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {
        long need = (long) target - a[i];
        if (need >= Integer.MIN_VALUE && need <= Integer.MAX_VALUE) {
            Integer j = seen.get((int) need);
            if (j != null) return new int[]{j, i};
        }
        seen.putIfAbsent(a[i], i);
    }
    return new int[0];
}
Worked result: [2,7,11,15], target 9 gives [0,1].
Time and space: O(n) expected time and O(n) space.
Edge-case policy: Repeated values are valid at different indices. No solution returns an empty array.
