24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C08
Top-k frequent words with deterministic ties
Return up to k words ordered by descending count and then ascending word. Reject
negative k.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Aggregate counts, then sort distinct entries with an explicit tie breaker. This clear baseline costs O(u
log u); a bounded heap improves very large u when k is small.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static List<String> topWords(List<String> words, int k) {
    if (k < 0) throw new IllegalArgumentException("negative k");
    Map<String, Long> freq = words.stream().collect(
        Collectors.groupingBy(Function.identity(), Collectors.counting()));
    return freq.entrySet().stream().sorted((a, b) -> {
        int c = Long.compare(b.getValue(), a.getValue());
        return c != 0 ? c : a.getKey().compareTo(b.getKey());
    }).limit(k).map(Map.Entry::getKey).collect(Collectors.toList());
}
Worked result: [b,a,b,a,c], k=2 gives [a,b].
Time and space: O(n + u log u) time, O(u) space before output.
Edge-case policy: k=0 returns empty; k greater than distinct count returns all; null words are excluded by the
input contract.
