24 PRACTICAL EXERCISES / JAVA 8 BASELINE
C09
Kth-largest value using a bounded heap
Return the kth-largest element, including duplicate occurrences, where 1 <= k <= n.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Maintain a min-heap containing the largest k values seen so far. Remove the smallest whenever the
heap exceeds k. Its head is the kth-largest value at completion.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static int kthLargest(int[] a, int k) {
    if (k < 1 || k > a.length) throw new IllegalArgumentException("k");
    PriorityQueue<Integer> heap = new PriorityQueue<>();
    for (int x : a) {
        heap.offer(x);
        if (heap.size() > k) heap.poll();
    }
    return heap.peek();
}
Worked result: [3,2,1,5,6,4], k=2 gives 5; [5,5,4], k=2 gives 5.
Time and space: O(n log(k+1)) time, O(k) heap space.
Edge-case policy: This is occurrence rank, not distinct rank. Invalid k rejects.
