LRU eviction in an access-order map
Implement a positive-capacity LRU map for single-threaded use. Reading an entry
refreshes its recency.
APPROACH - EASY EXPLANATION
Use LinkedHashMap access order and evict the eldest entry after insertion exceeds capacity. Declare
the concurrency and feature limits explicitly.
JAVA SOLUTION (REFERENCE METHOD)
static final class Lru<K,V> extends LinkedHashMap<K,V> {
    private final int capacity;
    Lru(int capacity) {
        super(16, 0.75f, true);
        if (capacity < 1) throw new IllegalArgumentException("capacity");
        this.capacity = capacity;
    }
    @Override protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<K,V> e) {
        return size() > capacity;
    }
}
