substring.
⚠ INTERVIEW PITFALL
Empty input returns empty; code-point semantics
require a different representation.
FOLLOW-UP QUESTION · ANSWERED
How does Manacher's algorithm reduce repeated expansion?
Manacher's algorithm reuses palindrome radii around mirrored centers and expands only when needed.
Insert conceptual separators to handle odd/even lengths uniformly. It finds the longest palindrome in O(n)
time.
JAVA 17 · SOLUTION Source Q018 · 13 lines
static String longestPalindrome(String text) {
  int start = 0, length = 0;
  for (int center = 0; center < text.length(); center++) {
    for (int even = 0; even <= 1; even++) {
      int l = center, r = center + even;
      while (l >= 0 && r < text.length() && text.charAt(l) == text.charAt(r)) {
        if (r-l+1 > length) { start = l; length = r-l+1; }
        l--; r++;
      }
    }
  }
  return text.substring(start, start + length);
}
