CHAPTER 24 · CONCURRENT PROGRAMMING TASKS QUESTION 117 / 120
Q117. Transfer integers through a bounded producer-
consumer queue.
✎  SIMPLE ANSWER
Use two owned workers and a bounded BlockingQueue. A reserved negative stop marker follows
all nonnegative values.
SKETCH THE PATTERN
EXAMPLE / INPUT
Values 1 through 100 ➜
KEY LOGIC
Use two owned workers and a
bounded BlockingQueue.
➜
RESULT
sum 5050
💡 FIFO places the terminal marker after every value from this single producer.
⏱ TIME & SPACE
Work O(n); queue space O(1) fixed capacity; two worker
resources.
⚠ INTERVIEW PITFALL
MAX_VALUE is rejected to avoid counter wrap; practical
n must finish within the exercise deadline.
FOLLOW-UP QUESTION · ANSWERED
How does termination change with several consumers?
Send one termination marker per consumer only after all producer work is complete, or use coordinated
interruption/queue close semantics. Otherwise one consumer may stop while others remain blocked
indefinitely.
JAVA 17 · SOLUTION Source Q117 · 15 lines
static long queueSum(int n) throws Exception {
  if(n<0 || n==Integer.MAX_VALUE) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
  BlockingQueue<Integer> queue=new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(8);
  ExecutorService pool=Executors.newFixedThreadPool(2);
  try {
    Future<Long> consumer=pool.submit(()-> {
      long total=0;
      while(true) { int x=queue.take(); if(x==-1) return total; total+=x; }
    });
    Future<?> producer=pool.submit(()-> {
      for(int i=1;i<=n;i++) queue.put(i); queue.put(-1); return null;
    });
    producer.get(5,TimeUnit.SECONDS); return consumer.get(5,TimeUnit.SECONDS);
  } finally { stopPool(pool); }
}
