pages.shortAnswer:
@BeforeEach runs setup before each test and @AfterEach runs cleanup after it. Keep
fixture creation local enough that readers can understand it; cleanup must not hide
failures.

assertTimeout executes on the calling thread and checks elapsed time afterward;
preemptive timeout can execute work in another thread and interrupt it. Preemptive
timeouts can disrupt thread-bound contexts.

@Tag can classify tests by purpose (unit, integration, slow); build tools and launchers
can include or exclude tags. Keep fast feedback separate from slower integration
coverage without hiding failures.

@Mock declares a mock field or parameter; MockitoExtension creates/cleans up
annotated mocks for JUnit Jupiter tests. Without initialization, a @Mock field can
remain null.

@SpringBootTest starts a Spring application context to exercise integration wiring. A
plain JUnit + Mockito test instantiates a service without Spring and is usually much
faster.

