JAVA 17 CODING LAB C02 COMPILED + EXECUTED
Bounded LRU cache
Full standalone source: Lab02.java · No framework dependencies · `javac --release 17 Lab02.java`
import java.util.*;
  public class Lab02 {
    static final class Lru<K,V> {
      private final int capacity;
      private final LinkedHashMap<K,V> data =
          new LinkedHashMap<>(16, 0.75f, true);
      Lru(int capacity) {
        if (capacity < 1) throw new IllegalArgumentException();
        this.capacity = capacity;
      }
      synchronized V get(K key) { return data.get(key); }
      synchronized void put(K key, V value) {
        Objects.requireNonNull(key); Objects.requireNonNull(value);
        data.put(key, value);
        if (data.size() > capacity)
          data.remove(data.keySet().iterator().next());
      }
      synchronized List<K> keys() { return List.copyOf(data.keySet()); }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
      var cache = new Lru<String,Integer>(2);
      cache.put("a", 1); cache.put("b", 2); cache.get("a");
      cache.put("c", 3);
      if (cache.get("b") != null) throw new AssertionError();
      if (!cache.keys().equals(List.of("a", "c")))
        throw new AssertionError();
      cache.put("a", 9);
      if (cache.get("a") != 9 || cache.keys().size() != 2)
        throw new AssertionError();
      System.out.println("b evicted; a retained; update does not grow cache");
    }
  }
VERIFIED OUTPUT
b evicted; a retained; update does not grow cache
Practice boundary: This proves the local model's included checks, not a durable multi-node production guarantee. Add
concurrency, failure-injection and integration tests before production use.
