pages.fullText:
JAVA 17 CODING LAB C12 COMPILED + EXECUTED
Outbox redelivery and local consumer deduplication
Full standalone source: Lab12.java · No framework dependencies · `javac --release 17 Lab12.java`
import java.util.*;
  public class Lab12 {
    record Event(String id, long amount) {}
    static final class ProducerModel {
      final List<Event> outbox = new ArrayList<>();
      int orders;
      synchronized void create(String eventId, long amount) {
        orders++; outbox.add(new Event(eventId, amount));
      }
    }
    static final class ConsumerModel {
      final Set<String> seen = new HashSet<>(); long total;
      synchronized boolean apply(Event event) {
        if (seen.contains(event.id())) return false;
        long next = Math.addExact(total, event.amount());
        seen.add(event.id()); total = next; return true;
      }
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
      var p = new ProducerModel(); var c = new ConsumerModel();
      p.create("e-1", 500);
      var event = p.outbox.get(0);
      if (!c.apply(event) || c.apply(event)) throw new AssertionError();
      if (c.total != 500 || c.seen.size() != 1 || p.orders != 1)
        throw new AssertionError();
      boolean overflow = false;
      try { c.apply(new Event("e-2", Long.MAX_VALUE)); }
      catch (ArithmeticException ex) { overflow = true; }
      if (!overflow || c.seen.contains("e-2") || c.total != 500)
        throw new AssertionError();
      System.out.println("duplicate e-1 ignored; total=500");
      System.out.println("failed effect does not store its dedup marker");
    }
  }
VERIFIED OUTPUT
duplicate e-1 ignored; total=500
failed effect does not store its dedup marker
Practice boundary: This proves the local model's included checks, not a durable multi-node production guarantee. Add
concurrency, failure-injection and integration tests before production use.
